@synopsis
**yume-gui** [ *options* ]
@end

## DESCRIPTION

**yume-gui** is an optional Dear ImGui desktop application. It embeds the same
facade sessions used by automation and tests: a man:yumed(8) server controller
and a linked, in-process man:yume(1) client runtime.

The GUI does not reimplement the transport stack. JSON profiles written here are
compatible with the CLI binaries.

## WORKSPACES

The sidebar switches between two workspaces:

@options
@opt **Client**
Connect, security, logs, settings, and credits for the man:yume(1) runtime.
@opt **Server**
Server control, authorized keys, logs, settings, and credits for man:yumed(8).
@end

## PAGES

@options
@opt **Dashboard**
Connection summary and quick status for the active workspace.
@opt **Connect**
Server host, identity key, SOCKS port, stealth toggles, and connect /
disconnect controls.
@opt **Security**
Inner crypto, TLS profile, obfs secret, and trust material (CA pins, operator
CA import).
@opt **Server**
Listen port, TLS cert paths, auth keys, real HTTP facade, and daemon
start/stop.
@opt **Keys**
Generate composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 identities and manage
**authorized_keys** entries.
@opt **Logs**
Live log view for the embedded client or server session.
@opt **Settings**
Appearance (theme), paths, and runtime preferences.
@opt **Credits**
Project version and license notice.
@end

## OPTIONS

@options
@opt **--headless**
Run a no-window facade diagnostic. It validates existing configuration files
and attempts start/stop for valid profiles. The current command still exits
successfully when profiles are absent or a valid session fails to start, so it
does not by itself verify a working connection.
@opt **--start-minimized**
Open hidden. Use the tray menu (when available) to show the main window.
@opt **--no-tray**
Disable the system tray icon at runtime even when the build includes tray
support.
@opt **--client-config** *path*
Load the client JSON profile from *path* instead of the platform default.
@opt **--server-config** *path*
Load the server JSON profile from *path* instead of the platform default.
@opt **-h, --help**
Print a help summary and exit.
@end

## KEYBOARD AND WINDOW

Standard Dear ImGui navigation applies: click fields to edit, Tab to move
focus, Enter to activate buttons. The main window can be resized; the
sidebar layout adapts to narrow widths.

There is no global accelerator table yet. Use the sidebar to switch pages.

## DEVELOPMENT STATUS

The dev6 GUI compiles and links, but it is not yet a qualified frontend. Shared
client/server lifecycle serialization, prompt pre-ready cancellation, and atomic
configuration replacement are covered by core/facade tests. Obsolete
inner-crypto controls/status, the GUI page's detached resolver lifetime, partial
chat/log delivery, honest headless failure behavior, and a real window-level
connect/stop/reconnect test remain GUI-owned work. Use the CLI for supported
automation and do not treat **--headless** as release evidence.

## SYSTEM TRAY

When tray support is compiled in and not disabled with **--no-tray**, a status
icon may appear in the desktop environment's notification area.

On Wayland (KDE Plasma, GNOME with certain compositors), tray behavior depends
on the desktop portal and StatusNotifier implementation. If the icon is missing,
run with **--no-tray** and keep the main window visible, or use the CLI binaries
directly.

## BUILD

The GUI is optional:

@code bash
./ezbuild.sh --gui
@end

Requires OpenGL, GLFW, and ImGui/ImPlot fetched by CMake. Debian packaging skips
the GUI when **DEB_BUILD_PROFILES** contains **nogui**.

## FILES

@options
@opt *~/.yume/client.json*
Default GUI client profile (Linux). macOS and Windows use the
platform-specific config directory under the user home.
@opt *~/.yume/server.json*
Default GUI server configuration.
@opt *~/.yume/secure-materials/*
Imported operator CAs, client auth keys, TLS CAs, and external proof keys. The
metadata uses schema 1 and 32-character random hex IDs. File paths are derived
from each record's ID and material type.
@opt *~/.yume/keys/*
Default key generation directory.
@end

